From ce65fa9fbdc3744b23921c66bad387e4af598f82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:23:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approvals): let decide_approval work from Telegram,
 checked in the database

guard_approval read auth.uid(), which is NULL for the service-role client that
Telegram uses, so every decision failed. Migration 0064 lets the service role
decide only when the row names a decided_by that is an owner, sales_leader or
deal_desk member of the approval's company. decide_approval now sets decided_by.
Signed-in users are checked exactly as before. Verified on PGlite (7 tests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
